 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Of course. Gluten free means chef's creativity, not necessarily worse than regular food. What do your roommate like and don't they eat? Ask them, they're usually happy to explain. Then each person can take the lead on a dish they' good at. Pasta, bread, cakes, some sauces. Anything with gluten needs signs warning of cross contamination. Then find a gluten free brand. There are good ones that taste more like real food than you' think. Avocado sauce is also simple and lovely. It is sad that gluten makes people feel so cut off. You could all go out together for something she can eat.",
